65 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 52 0 R
/T (For a new office PC, I would first decide the CPU according to the work: Microsoft Office, web browsing, accounting software, video meetings and multitasking. Then I would choose a motherboard that supports the CPU socket, CPU generation and chipset. After that, I would select RAM that matches the motherboard, such as the correct DDR generation and supported speed. Finally, I would choose storage based on the available M.2/NVMe or SATA interface and required capacity.)
/E (For a new office PC, I would first decide the CPU according to the work: Microsoft Office, web browsing, accounting software, video meetings and multitasking. Then I would choose a motherboard that supports the CPU socket, CPU generation and chipset. After that, I would select RAM that matches the motherboard, such as the correct DDR generation and supported speed. Finally, I would choose storage based on the available M.2/NVMe or SATA interface and required capacity.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
