69 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 52 0 R
/T (An HDD uses spinning magnetic disks. It gives large capacity at a low cost, but it is slower. A SATA SSD uses flash memory and has no moving parts, so booting and application loading are much faster. An NVMe SSD also uses flash memory, but it communicates over PCIe, giving higher bandwidth and lower latency than a traditional SATA SSD.)
/E (An HDD uses spinning magnetic disks. It gives large capacity at a low cost, but it is slower. A SATA SSD uses flash memory and has no moving parts, so booting and application loading are much faster. An NVMe SSD also uses flash memory, but it communicates over PCIe, giving higher bandwidth and lower latency than a traditional SATA SSD.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
